      whenNotToUse: 'Don\'t use "delegate" when you\'re simply asking someone for help casually. "Can you delegate me a sandwich?" makes no sense. Also, delegation implies a hierarchical relationship — peers don\'t typically "delegate" to each other; they "share" or "distribute" work.',
      culturalContext: 'In Western management philosophy, effective delegation is considered a hallmark of good leadership. It empowers team members, develops their skills, and allows leaders to focus on strategic priorities. Failure to delegate is often seen as a weakness, not a strength.'
